														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2032762">
									

<p>Kalinin words it better than I could have. Unlike him, I was unfazed by the technical things in his line-by-line, but the article completely lost me at &quot;Subjects in the town of ███████ universally believe that they have to &quot;get out of town&quot; and not return.&quot;</p>
<p>Aside from his complaint of inserting prose into quotes in a clinical document (that being a major peeve of mine as well), overall this touches on another big thing that I strongly dislike&#8212;-homogeny.</p>
<p>Compulsion is mental/psychological. Not all people are identical, not just in terms of psyche but in actual brain chemistry and structure sometimes. If you poke a hole in the exact same spot in 100 people's brains, you're not going to have 100 identical psychological results (other than maybe 100 severe migraines or death by hole in the brain).</p>
<p>Having everyone just universally go &quot;Ew I must leave&quot; comes across as completely artificial and in no way realistic</p>

